<title>BRAZIL: Brazil govt sells 92 pct of coffee at auction.</title>
<headline>Brazil govt sells 92 pct of coffee at auction.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government sold around 92 percent, or 137,808 60-kg bags, of the 149,705 bags of coffee stocks offered to all segments of the coffee sector in its auction today, according to Banco do Brasil.</p>
<p>Total revenue for the government was 18.97 million reais ($17.56 million).</p>
<p>Closing prices were up to eight reais higher than opening levels set by the government.</p>
<p>Opening and closing prices in reais per bag per lot were as follows.</p>
<p> QTY	CROP	COLOR	LOCATION		PRICE</p>
<p>					(STATE)	   OPENING  CLOSING</p>
<p> 22,890   1986/87   Yellowish   MG		   139   146.60</p>
<p>  9,500   1987/88   Yellowish   MG		   134	138</p>
<p> 11,415   1987/88   Greenish    PR		   139   142.50</p>
<p> 16,710   1987/88   Yellowish   PR		   132	132</p>
<p> 13,140   1987/88   Whitish     PR		   132	132</p>
<p>  8,530   1987/88   Yellowish   PR		   132	132</p>
<p> 10,000   1987/88   Light green PR		   139   139.30</p>
<p> 24,530   1987/88   Yellowish   SP		   134   134.55</p>
<p>    760							134   134.85</p>
<p>  6,998   1987/88   Yellowish   SP		   134	142</p>
<p>  2,966   1987/88   Yellowish   SP		   139	144</p>
<p> 10,369   1987/88   Yellowish   SP		   134   134.05</p>
<p>TOTAL - 137,808 bags</p>
<p>The next auction is scheduled for August 6.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
